---
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import CommonLayout from "../layouts/CommonLayout.astro";
import OneColumn from "../components/OneColumn.astro";
import Note from "../components/Note.astro";
import LocationDusVenue from "../components/LocationDusVenue.astro";
import LocationDusRooms from "../components/LocationDusRooms.astro";
import UnconfSchedule from "../components/schedule/UnconfSchedule.astro";
import UnconfSponsors from "../components/unconf/UnconfSponsors.astro";
import UnconfGroups from "../components/unconf/UnconfGroups.astro";
import UnconfLeaders from "../components/unconf/UnconfLeaders.astro";
import HeroAnchors from "src/components/HeroAnchors.astro";
import Divider from "src/components/Divider.astro";
import Markdown from "src/components/Markdown.astro";

const unconfIntro = await Astro.glob("./unconf-intro.md");
---

<CommonLayout title="Unconf participants guide" ogDescription="Guide for participants of the RustWeek unconference">
  <Hero title="Unconf participants guide" color="yellow">
    <HeroAnchors>
      <a href="#venue">Venue</a> &bullet;
      <a href="#unconf-details">Schedule</a> &bullet;
      <a href="#rooms">Rooms</a> &bullet;
      <a href="#all-hands">All-Hands</a> &bullet;
      <a href="#sponsors">Sponsors</a> &bullet;
      <a href="#group-leaders">Group leaders</a> &bullet;
      <a href="#grants">Grants</a> &bullet;
      <a href="#travel">Travel</a> &bullet;
    </HeroAnchors>
  </Hero>
  <OneColumn>
    <div class="markdown" set:html={unconfIntro[0].compiledContent()} />
    <br />
    <div class="markdown">
      <Note>
        <p>
          NOTE: All information on this page is for invited participants of the
          unconf. If you are not invited by one of the unconf groups, please
          check out the <a href="/">homepage</a> for all RustWeek events.
        </p>
      </Note>
    </div>
  </OneColumn>
  <UnconfGroups />
      <OneColumn >
        <Divider />
    </OneColumn>
  <OneColumn>
      <Markdown>
      <h2 id="venue">The unconference venue</h2>
      <p>
        The unconf is held at DUS Utrecht.<br />
        Address: DUS, Sophialaan 1, Utrecht, The Netherlands.
      </p>
      <p>
        See the <a href="/dus">DUS venue page</a> on how to reach the Venue, and the <a href="/bus">DUS BUS page</a> for the bus departure times.
      </p>
    </Markdown>
  </OneColumn>
  <LocationDusVenue />
  <div class="space-y-12">
    <UnconfSchedule />
  </div>
  <OneColumn>
    <div class="markdown">
      <h2 id="unconf-details">Unconf Schedule (Thu, Fri and Sat)</h2>
      <p>
        Schedule for all days:<br />
        <ul style="font-family: monospace;font-size: smaller;">
          <li>09:00 - 09:30: Arrival and registration</li>
          <li>09:30 - 13:30: Unconf sessions</li>
          <li>13:30 - 14:30: Lunch</li>
          <li>14:30 - 17:30: Unconf sessions</li>
          <li>17:30 - 18:30: Drinks & departure from the venue</li>
        </ul>
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Covid policy:</b> Please review our <a
          href="/covid-policy-all-hands-and-unconf">covid policy</a
        > for the unconf.
      </p>
      <p>
        For questions about logistics or other, your <a href="#group-leaders"
          >group leader</a
        > can reach out to Erik via erik@rustnl.org, or join the <a
          href="https://discord.gg/FSwaWZdk6k ">RustWeek discord</a
        > and ask there.
      </p>
    </div>
  </OneColumn>
  <OneColumn>
    <Divider />
  </OneColumn>
  <UnconfSponsors />

  <OneColumn>
    <Divider />
  </OneColumn>

  <div class="space-y-12" id="floorplan">
    <OneColumn>
      <Markdown>
        <h2>Venue layout</h2>
        <p>
          The venue has a socializing and outdoor area, the All-Hands wing (see below, in pink)
          and the Unconference wing (green). More information can be found on the <a
          href="/dus#floor-plan">DUS venue page</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p>
          The venue has 20+ airconditioned rooms, of which 10 are reserved for the unconf.
          For lunch and socializing there are big inside and outside areas.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each unconf group will have a main room and a breakout room. The rooms
          will have tables made out of cardboard that you can write on, a
          flipover, and each group's main room has a large HDMI screen.
        </p>
        
      <h2 id="rooms">Room assignments</h2>

      <div style="overflow-y: scroll;margin: 0 -16px;">
      <table style="text-align: center; border: 1px solid #ccc;">
        <tr
          style="font-weight: bold; border: 1px solid #ccc;"
        >
          <th>Room</th>
          <th>Breakout</th>
          <th>Thu</th>
          <th>Fri</th>
          <th>Sat</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>1</td>
          <td>1A, 1B</td>
          <td>Bevy</td>
          <td>Bevy</td>
          <td>Bevy</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>4</td>
          <td>3</td>
          <td >Rust Embedded </td>
          <td><i>Free</i></td>
          <td><i>Free</i></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>5</td>
          <td>6</td>
          <td>Linebender</td>
          <td>GPU</td>
          <td><i>Free</i></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>8</td>
          <td>-</td>
          <td><i>Free</i></td>
          <td><i>Free</i></td>
          <td><i>Free</i></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>9</td>
          <td>-</td>
          <td>ArielOS</td>
          <td><i>Free</i></td>
          <td><i>Free</i></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>11</td>
          <td>10</td>
          <td>Safety-Critical</td>
          <td>Rust Embedded </td>
          <td>Rust Embedded </td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      </div>
      <style>
        th,
        td {
          padding: 5px;
          border: 1px solid #ccc; 
          border-width;: 0px 1px;

          font-size: 0.9rem;

          i {
            color: #888;
          }
        }
      </style>
      <p>
        Please note that breakout rooms 3 and 6 do <strong>not</strong>
        have a screen.
      </p>
      <p>
        Rooms 2 and 7 are reserved for RustNL.
      </p>
      </Markdown>
    </OneColumn>
    <div class="container">
      <img
        style="margin: 2rem 0rem;width:100%;"
        src="/images/venues/dus-floorplan.png"
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <UnconfLeaders />

  <OneColumn>
    <div class="markdown">
      <h2 id="all-hands">Co-located Rust All Hands</h2>
      <p>
        At the same venue, in the other wing of the same buliding, there will be
        a parallel event: the Rust All Hands. Collaboration is encouraged! Feel
        free to invite Rust project members to your sessions. If you want to
        join any of the sessions of the Rust All-Hands, or if you want to
        organize joint sessions, ask Mara, via Zulip or mara@rustnl.org. She
        coordinates the Rust All-Hands. Please also respect the private nature
        of the Rust All-Hands sessions; do not walk into the All-Hands wing and
        sessions uninvited.
      </p>
    </div>
  </OneColumn>
  <LocationDusRooms />

  <OneColumn>
    <div class="markdown">
      <h2 id="travel">Travel and Hotel</h2>
      <p>
        See the <a href="/getting-there">Getting there page</a> for details on travel
        to Utrecht.
      </p>
      <p>
        For hotel recommendations see our <a href="/hotels">hotels page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="grants">Grants</h2>
      <p>
        RustNL can help cover part of cost for travel and stay for upto 3
        participants in each unconf group.<br /><br />The compensation is
        reserved for participants that are not covered by their employer or
        other sponsor, and need the support to be able to participate. The compensation is capped at EUR 500 plus a conference ticket per participant.
        Please contact your <a href="#group-leaders">group's leader(s)</a> to be nominated for a grant.
      </p>
      <h2 id="questions">Questions?</h2>
      <p>
        If you have any logistical or organisational questions, please reach out
        to Erik via erik@rustnl.org.
      </p>
    </div>
  </OneColumn>
</CommonLayout>
